The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (error) {
    put_device(&sdkp->disk_dev);
    goto out;
}
```
Reason: When `device_add(&sdkp->disk_dev)` fails, `put_device(&sdkp->disk_dev)` is called, which triggers `scsi_disk_release()` to free the `scsi_disk` structure (`sdkp`). However, the `gendisk` (`gd`) still holds an extra reference from earlier allocation, and this path does not release it via `put_disk(gd)`. This causes a memory leak of the `gendisk`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (error) {
    put_device(&sdkp->disk_dev);
    put_disk(gd);
    goto out;
}
```
Reason: Adding `put_disk(gd)` after `put_device(&sdkp->disk_dev)` ensures that the reference count on the `gendisk` is properly decremented when `device_add(&sdkp->disk_dev)` fails. This mirrors the cleanup done later in the `device_add_disk()` error path (which also calls `put_disk(gd)`), preventing the memory leak of the `gendisk`.

